          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.425,
            0.462,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Bridging Science and Society"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.464,
            0.748,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Yoga, described in ancient Indian texts includes physical postures, breathing and meditation. Research shows it improves flexibility, posture and breathing, reduces stress, and helps prevent lifestyle diseases. Every year, 21st June is observed as the International Yoga Day to promote role of Yoga in health and well-being."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.544,
            0.747,
            0.592
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Maintaining correct posture, proper nutrition, regular exercise and yoga keeps our bones strong, muscles fit, joints flexible, and protects the body from stiffness."
            }
          ]
        },
